<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20906] LFSCK: recreating a lost MDT object loses EC layout semantics</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20906</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When an EC file's MDT object is lost,  lfsck_layout_recreate_parent() → new_comp_lovea()&lt;br/&gt;
rebuilds components with only LCME_FL_INIT/RAID0,  then dropping parity semantics.&lt;br/&gt;
The root cause is that the "struct ost_layout" on OST object carries no EC fields.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
